{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"edits\":[{\"field\":\"history/1/text\",\"text\":\"Two Shang graphs made from 門 and 口 were traditionally read as 問, but their identification and descent from the later 問 graph remain disputed. One tentative alternative treats them as expanded forms of 啟; their inscriptional meaning is unclear. The received Shuowen analysis of the later form does not settle this earlier reading.\"},{\"field\":\"meaning_history/senses/0/text\",\"text\":\"The use of 問 meaning “ask” or “inquire” is reported in late Warring States Qin slips. This is the earliest clear graph for that use in the evidence discussed here; it does not establish that the spoken word began then or that asking was its original meaning.\"},{\"field\":\"relationships/3/text\",\"text\":\"問 has the established use “ask” or “inquire,” reported for late Warring States Qin slips. This relationship represents that attested use; whether it was the word’s original meaning is unresolved.\"}]}"}}
